        "origin": "authoring_observation",
        "status": "suspected",
        "classification": "defect",
        "description": "The tighter multi-GEMM cap expands the range that produces zero blocks and reaches integer division by zero.",
        "trigger": "For example, automatic Ampere multi-GEMM with K=512, N=128 and bits=2 selects shape 2, giving 16 tiles and num_sms=0 under division by 24; the previous division by 12 gave one block.",
        "expected_behavior": "A nonempty supported matrix should receive a positive block count or be rejected before concurrency arithmetic.",
        "actual_behavior": "exl3_mgemm computes total_sms / num_sms without a zero guard. Direct Python callers occur in attention's fused K/V projection and the fused expert gate/up/down path; their inspected call sites do not enforce a minimum tile count. This does not establish that typical model dimensions trigger the condition.",
        "locations": [
